  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `_withdraw()` function in `StakingBase` (lines 929-948) reads the `balance` state variable into a local variable at the start, makes multiple external ETH transfers in a loop via `_transfer()`, and only writes the updated balance back to storage **after all transfers complete**. For `StakingNativeToken`, each `_transfer()` call sends ETH via `to.call{value: amount}(\"\")` (line 29), giving execution control to the recipient.\n\n**Vulnerable code in StakingBase.sol (lines 929-948):**\n```solidity\nfunction _withdraw(address[] memory receivers, uint256[] memory amounts) internal virtual {\n    uint256 updatedBalance = balance;                    // LINE 931 - reads balance\n    for (uint256 i = 0; i < receivers.length; ++i) {\n        updatedBalance -= amounts[i];                    // LINE 938 - local decrement\n        _transfer(receivers[i], amounts[i]);             // LINE 941 - EXTERNAL CALL (ETH)\n        emit Withdraw(receivers[i], amounts[i]);\n    }\n    balance = updatedBalance;                            // LINE 947 - writes AFTER all calls\n}\n```\n\n**StakingNativeToken._transfer() (lines 27-33) sends ETH:**\n```solidity\nfunction _transfer(address to, uint256 amount) internal override {\n    (bool success, ) = to.call{value: amount}(\"\");  // Gives execution control to `to`\n    if (!success) {\n        revert TransferFailed(address(0), address(this), to, amount);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nIf a reward recipient re-enters the staking contract during `_transfer()` (e.g., by calling `claim()` for a **different** service they own), the inner `_withdraw()` reads the **stale** `balance` from storage (outer hasn't written yet). When the outer `_withdraw()` resumes, it **overwrites** the inner write with its own stale local variable, permanently corrupting the `balance` accounting.\n\n**Attack scenario:**\n\n1. Attacker owns two services (A and B), both staked in the same `StakingNativeToken` contract. Both use `RewardDistributionType.ServiceOwner`. Contract `balance = 100 ETH`.\n\n2. Attacker calls `unstake(serviceA)` which triggers `_withdraw()`:\n   - **Outer `_withdraw()`**: reads `updatedBalance = 100` from storage.\n   - `updatedBalance -= 5` → local `updatedBalance = 95`.\n   - `_transfer(attacker, 5 ETH)` sends ETH to attacker's contract.\n\n3. **Attacker's `receive()` triggers**, calling `claim(serviceB)`:\n   - **Inner `_withdraw()`**: reads `updatedBalance = 100` from storage (**STALE!**).\n   - `updatedBalance -= 5` → inner local `updatedBalance = 95`.\n   - `_transfer(victim, 5 ETH)` sends 5 ETH.\n   - **Inner writes `balance = 95`** to storage.\n\n4. **Outer `_withdraw()` resumes**:\n   - Writes **`balance = 95`** to storage (its own stale local).\n   - **Overwrites** the inner write.\n\n5. **Result**:\n   - Contract sent out **10 ETH** total (5 + 5).\n   - But `balance = 95` instead of correct `90`.\n   - **Contract is insolvent**: recorded balance > actual ETH.\n   - All remaining stakers who try to withdraw amounts that exceed actual ETH will be permanently DoS'd.\n\n**Note on reentrancy guard**: Neither `_claim()`, `_unstake()`, `_withdraw()`, nor `_stake()` have reentrancy guards. The comment on line 564 says \"the reentrancy is not possible since the reward is set to zero\" — but this only prevents re-claiming the **same** service. Claiming a **different** service owned by the same attacker is not prevented.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n**Option 1 (Preferred)**: Update `balance` in storage **before each transfer**, not after the loop:\n\n```solidity\nfunction _withdraw(address[] memory receivers, uint256[] memory amounts) internal virtual {\n    for (uint256 i = 0; i < receivers.length; ++i) {\n        balance -= amounts[i];  // Update storage BEFORE external call\n        _transfer(receivers[i], amounts[i]);\n        emit Withdraw(receivers[i], amounts[i]);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Option 2**: Add a reentrancy guard to `_withdraw`, `_claim`, `_unstake`, and `_stake`:\n\n```solidity\nuint256 internal _locked = 1;\n\nmodifier nonReentrant() {\n    require(_locked == 1, \"Reentrancy\");\n    _locked = 2;\n    _;\n    _locked = 1;\n}\n```",
